+# ajv vs zod: validating draft 2020-12 JSON Schema documents (Node)
+
+Question: [QUESTION.md](../QUESTION.md). Date: 2026-11-11.
+
+> **Evidence status: none of this was checked against a source in this run.**
+> The repo has no `node_modules` (no `package.json`; Glob found no `ajv`/`zod` under the repo, `/usr` or `/root`). WebFetch of the official docs was not permitted. Every claim below is **inferred** from prior knowledge of these libraries. Each one names the primary source that should confirm it before anyone relies on it.
+
+## Short answer
+
+**Use ajv.** It is a JSON Schema validator and supports draft 2020-12 directly. Zod is a TypeScript-first schema library. It does not validate data against an arbitrary JSON Schema document. Zod 4 can *export* JSON Schema (including 2020-12) from Zod schemas. Any JSON Schema → Zod import is a conversion helper, not a 2020-12 validator.
+
+## ajv
+
+| Claim | Status | Source to verify |
+|---|---|---|
+| Supports drafts 04/06/07, 2019-09 and 2020-12 (and JTD) | inferred | https://ajv.js.org/json-schema.html, https://ajv.js.org/guide/schema-language.html |
+| 2020-12 needs the separate class `import Ajv2020 from "ajv/dist/2020"`. The default `ajv` export targets draft-07. | inferred | same pages; `node_modules/ajv/dist/2020.js` once installed |
+| 2020-12 keywords (`prefixItems`, `$dynamicRef`/`$dynamicAnchor`, `unevaluatedProperties`/`unevaluatedItems`) are implemented | inferred | https://ajv.js.org/json-schema.html (draft 2020-12 section) |
+| One Ajv instance cannot mix draft-2020-12 and draft-07 schemas | inferred | https://ajv.js.org/guide/schema-language.html |
+| `format` validation needs the `ajv-formats` plugin | inferred | https://ajv.js.org/guide/formats.html |
+
+Usage (inferred, v8):
+```js
+import Ajv2020 from "ajv/dist/2020.js";
+const ajv = new Ajv2020();
+const validate = ajv.compile(schema); // schema.$schema = "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"
+validate(data) || console.log(validate.errors);
+```
+
+## zod
+
+| Claim | Status | Source to verify |
+|---|---|---|
+| Zod validates data against **Zod schemas** defined in TS/JS, not against JSON Schema documents | inferred | https://zod.dev |
+| Zod 4 has `z.toJSONSchema()`, which outputs draft 2020-12 by default (draft-07 by option) | inferred | https://zod.dev/json-schema |
+| Zod 3 had no built-in JSON Schema support. Third-party `zod-to-json-schema` / `json-schema-to-zod` filled the gap. | inferred | https://zod.dev (v3 docs), npm pages of those packages |
+| Any `z.fromJSONSchema()` in recent Zod 4 is experimental and does not claim full 2020-12 coverage | **open**: not confirmed this exists | https://zod.dev/json-schema, Zod changelog |
+
